<Base title="Our Story" description="Why Willing Spirit Animal Sanctuary exists, and our vision for connecting rescued animals with children who have experienced trauma.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="narrow prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Our story</p>
      <h1>Rescue. Heal. Connect.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Willing Spirit Animal Sanctuary began with a simple belief: healing can start with something as small as a child sitting beside an animal that trusts them.</p>

      <!-- TODO(Tess): A few paragraphs in your own words — how you got into rescue, and why this matters to you. -->
      <p>Our founder, Tess, cares for rescued dogs in foster care in the Raleigh area, giving animals who have known neglect, abandonment or uncertainty the time, patience and veterinary care they need to become whole again.</p>

      <h2>What we do today</h2>
      <p>Right now, our work is animal rescue: fostering vulnerable animals, getting them the medical care and training they need, and helping them find safe, loving homes. Every donation, supply, and volunteer hour goes toward that care.</p>

      <h2>Where we're headed</h2>
      <div class="notice"><strong>Please note:</strong> the programs below are our vision for the future. They are not yet operating.</div>
      <p style="margin-top:1rem">Children in foster care often face abuse, neglect, instability and separation from the people they love. Many find it hard to trust adults, yet may feel safe sitting beside, grooming, walking or caring for an animal.</p>
      <p>We plan to carefully evaluate rescued animals for temperament, health and suitability, give them rehabilitation and training, and develop them into safe, compassionate partners for <strong>supervised animal-assisted activities</strong> with children who have experienced trauma, especially children in foster care and families with limited resources.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Built with professionals.</strong> We intend to partner with foster families, social-service agencies, schools, counselors and therapists. Our programs will complement, never replace, professional mental-health care.</li>
        <li><strong>Safe by design.</strong> Animal screening, trained staff and volunteers, child-protection procedures, and trauma-informed practice will come first.</li>
        <li><strong>Accessible.</strong> Wherever possible, activities will be free, subsidized or scholarship-supported.</li>
        <li><strong>Never forced.</strong> Every child moves at their own pace, with patience, choice, predictability and respect.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>A shared second chance</h2>
      <p>A rescued animal learning that people can be safe. A child learning to trust again. When the two come together, each can show the other what resilience looks like. That's the heart of Willing Spirit.</p>
      <p><a class="btn" href="/get-involved/">Help us get there</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
